---
import BusinessFooter from "@/components/landing/BusinessFooter.astro";
import SiteHeader from "@/components/SiteHeader.astro";
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import { siteNavItems } from "@/utils/site-nav";
import "@/styles/business.css";
import "@/styles/service.css";

const navItems = siteNavItems();

const updated = "23 August 2026";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy · Tomer Gal"
  description="What this site measures, what it does not, and how to ask for any of it to be removed."
>
  <div class="business-site service-page">
    <SiteHeader
      homeHref="/"
      homeLabel="Tomer Gal home"
      mainId="privacy-main"
      navAriaLabel="Services navigation"
      navItems={navItems}
      variant="business"
    />

    <main id="privacy-main">
      <section class="business-section service-hero">
        <div class="business-wrap">
          <span class="business-eyebrow">Privacy</span>
          <h1>What this site measures.</h1>
          <p class="service-lede">
            Short version: anonymous page counts, and which buttons get clicked. No cookies, no accounts,
            no tracking you across other websites.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <hr class="business-rule" />

      <section class="business-section">
        <div class="business-wrap">
          <div class="business-section-head">
            <div>
              <span class="business-eyebrow">What is collected</span>
              <h2>Anonymous traffic, and a handful of clicks.</h2>
            </div>
          </div>
          <ul class="service-list service-list--deliverable">
            <li>Pages viewed, plus the country, browser and device type your browser reports.</li>
            <li>The site that linked you here, if any, and any campaign tags in the link you followed.</li>
            <li>
              Clicks on a small number of things I care about: booking a call, my email address, opening a
              service page, and following a link from an article to a service.
            </li>
            <li>Page loading speed, so I can tell when the site gets slower.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="service-pricing-note">
            This runs on Vercel Web Analytics and Vercel Speed Insights. Vercel does not use cookies for
            this and does not build a cross-site profile of you. Campaign tags and the referring site are
            kept in your browser for the length of your visit and are cleared when you close the tab.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <hr class="business-rule" />

      <section class="business-section">
        <div class="business-wrap">
          <div class="business-section-head">
            <div>
              <span class="business-eyebrow">What is not</span>
              <h2>Deliberately not collected.</h2>
            </div>
          </div>
          <ul class="service-triggers">
            <li class="service-trigger">No cookies are set by this site.</li>
            <li class="service-trigger">No fingerprinting, and no attempt to identify you personally.</li>
            <li class="service-trigger">No advertising networks, and no data sold or shared for advertising.</li>
            <li class="service-trigger">No session recording, heatmaps, or A/B testing.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <hr class="business-rule" />

      <section class="business-section">
        <div class="business-wrap">
          <div class="business-section-head">
            <div>
              <span class="business-eyebrow">When you get in touch</span>
              <h2>Email and booking.</h2>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="business-reveal">
            <p class="service-next-body">
              If you email me or book a call, I keep what you send me: your name, your email address, and
              whatever you tell me about your situation, so I can reply and, if we work together, do the
              work. I keep a short private record of where enquiries came from so I know which writing is
              worth continuing. Emailing me does not put you on a mailing list, and I do not pass any of
              it on.
            </p>
            <p class="service-next-note">
              Calls are booked through Google Calendar, which has its own privacy policy and collects its
              own data once you land there.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <hr class="business-rule" />

      <section class="business-section">
        <div class="business-wrap">
          <div class="business-section-head">
            <div>
              <span class="business-eyebrow">If you sign up for it</span>
              <h2>The newsletter.</h2>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="business-reveal">
            <p class="service-next-body">
              There are four letters, one for each service, and the only way to get one is to ask for it
              on the form yourself. Signing up stores your email address and which letters you chose.
              Nothing else, and nothing you have not typed into the form.
            </p>
            <p class="service-next-body">
              The letters do record whether you opened them and which links you clicked. I use it to
              work out which subjects were worth writing about, and nothing else. It is the one place on
              this site where something is measured against you rather than anonymously, so it is worth
              saying plainly. If you would rather it did not, tell me and I will turn it off for your
              address.
            </p>
            <p class="service-next-body">
              Every letter has a link at the bottom that lets you change which ones you get, or stop all
              of them. It takes one click, it works without me, and you do not need to give a reason.
            </p>
            <p class="service-next-note">
              The letters are sent through Resend, which stores the address on my behalf and has its own
              privacy policy. I do not pass it on to anyone else.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <hr class="business-rule" />

      <section class="business-section">
        <div class="business-wrap">
          <div class="business-section-head">
            <div>
              <span class="business-eyebrow">Your call</span>
              <h2>Asking me to delete it.</h2>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="business-reveal">
            <p class="service-next-body">
              Email me and I will delete whatever I hold about you, and tell you when it is done. You do
              not need to give a reason. If your browser sends a Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control
              signal, no analytics events are recorded for your visit.
            </p>
            <p class="service-next-note">Last updated {updated}.</p>
          </div>
          <a class="business-mail" href="mailto:tomer.wave@gmail.com">tomer.wave@gmail.com</a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <BusinessFooter />
  </div>
</Layout>
